title: slot:show
tags: [[GUI command]] [[Panel slots and layout]]
kind: reference
summary: Show a panel type in a named slot, and in a viewer a file

`slot:show <left|right> <type> [path]` shows a panel type in a slot named outright,
whichever holds the focus, without moving the focus. A hidden slot is shown first; one
with no workspace takes the focused slot's, and it fails when there is none. It is what
[[mf gui view]] runs; [[panel:open]], which goes by the focused slot, is the one for a key.

`path` counts only with `viewer`, and selects that file in the slot's workspace:

* a path sets `selected_metarecord` to the metarecord at that path — `null` for an untracked file, or when the daemon does not answer — and `selected_paths` to `[path]`;
* no `path` leaves the selection as it is;
* an ''empty'' `path` clears both. A script previewing the entry it asks about reaches entries with no file, and leaving the previous file on screen would present it as the subject of the question.

It runs in a [[transaction|Command transactions]], unlike the other builtins: the pair is
delivered together, once the slot has changed — so a refused slot leaves the selection
as it was. The selection moving this way asks nothing about an unsaved edit
([[Edits in progress]]). Unlike [[panel:open]], it opens a viewer whatever the selection.

An invocation typed as a line cannot say an empty path: a script sends the words as an
array ([[GUI scripting endpoints]]).
